Parseomatic bundles the following third-party assets:

Material Design Icons (https://pictogrammers.com/library/mdi/)
  The `sword` and `bow-arrow` glyph outlines used for role icons in the
  Overview players table (src/ui/widgets/role-icon.ts), and the
  `sword-cross` / `heart-plus` / `grave-stone` / `shoe-print` / `chart-timeline`
  / `head-remove` / `timetable` (Nerd Fonts aliases `nf-md-grave_stone` /
  `nf-md-shoe_print` / `nf-md-chart_timeline` / `nf-md-head_remove` /
  `nf-md-timetable`) toolbar icons for the Damage / Healing / Deaths /
  Movement / Timeline / Interrupts / Raid views (index.html), and
  the `filter-variant` glyph used for the Timeline view's per-lane ability
  filter (src/ui/widgets/timeline-lanes.ts), and the `code-json` glyph
  (Nerd Fonts alias `nf-md-code_json`) used for the Encounter Editor's
  JSON-view toggle button (index.html).
  Copyright Pictogrammers contributors.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

Octicons (https://primer.style/octicons/)
  The `plug` glyph outline (Nerd Fonts alias `nf-oct-plug`) used for the
  toolbar's "open data folder" button (index.html), and the `git-branch`
  glyph outline used for the Encounter Editor's "Tidy" button (index.html;
  substituted for the requested `nf-dev-git_branch`, which has no
  fetchable vector source -- Nerd Fonts patches it in from a font file,
  not published SVG).
  Copyright GitHub, Inc.
  Licensed under the MIT License (https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT).

Codicons (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-codicons)
  The `new-file`, `file`, and `save` glyph outlines (Nerd Fonts aliases
  `nf-cod-new_file` / `nf-cod-file` / `nf-cod-save`) used for the Encounter
  Editor's New / Open / Save toolbar buttons (index.html).
  Copyright Microsoft Corporation.
  Icon designs licensed under CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/) -- the codicons font-build
  tooling itself is separately MIT-licensed, but that license doesn't cover
  the icon artwork.

Font Awesome Free (https://fontawesome.com)
  The `bandage` glyph outline (Nerd Fonts alias `nf-fa-bandage`) used for
  the Damage Taken character view's toolbar icon, and the `video` glyph
  outline (Nerd Fonts alias `nf-fa-video_camera`) used for the Replay
  view's toolbar icon (index.html).
  Copyright Fonticons, Inc.
  Icons licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
